cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "Add Health ERGM Analysis: Supplemental materials for suicidal ideation and adolescent friendship networks"
message: >-
  If you use this analysis code or these supplemental results, please cite
  this repository. The associated manuscript is "Populations to Social
  Networks: Identifying structural effects of suicidal ideation on adolescent
  friendship networks".
authors:
  - family-names: McDonnell Maayan
    given-names: Gabe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5725-7622"
  - family-names: Gondal
    given-names: Neha
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7337-9072"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gabemgem/Add-Health-ERGM-Analysis"
url: "https://github.com/gabemgem/Add-Health-ERGM-Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R analysis code and supplemental results accompanying research
  on suicidal ideation and adolescent friendship networks in the National
  Longitudinal Study of Adolescent to Adult Health (Add Health). Includes
  directed exponential random graph models (ERGMs), separable temporal ERGMs
  of friendship formation and persistence between Waves I and II, community
  descriptives, model diagnostics, and exploratory pooling and sensitivity
  analyses. Restricted-use respondent-level data are not included.
